What is ours
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Of the icons in `web/src/shared/ui/icon.tsx`: none. Every one of the sixteen is Feather's,
and the table above is exhaustive -- `FEATHER_SOURCE` in that file maps every member of
`IconName` to a Feather file, so an icon with no Feather source does not currently
typecheck.

Ours is the `Icon` component around them: the attribute convention, the sizing prop, the
`aria-hidden`-by-default rule and the names. That code is part of this repository and
carries this repository's licence.

A later session that needs an icon Feather does not have should draw it, widen
`FEATHER_SOURCE` to admit an icon of our own, and add a row here saying so. It must not
pass off a drawing as Feather's, and it must not reconstruct a Feather path from memory --
the sixteen above were fetched from the source and pasted, which is why they can be
compared against it.

`web/tests/unit/icon-convention.test.ts` reads this file and fails if the table and
`FEATHER_SOURCE` stop agreeing, so this notice cannot silently fall behind the set.

The copy itself is checked too. `web/tests/unit/icon-feather-source.ts` holds every
Feather document as it was fetched, each with the `sha256` of the fetched bytes, and
`web/tests/unit/icon-provenance.test.ts` compares what the component renders against them.
A path edited after the fact would make this notice wrong about what was copied, which is
the failure `D-52` was opened over, so it fails the suite instead.
